        <div id="faq" class="scroll-mt-24 mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            10. Frequently Asked Questions
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the best sub compact tractor?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                For most buyers, the Kubota BX2680: 19.5 claimed PTO hp, a hydrostatic 4WD drivetrain, a Category I hitch and Kubota's dealer network. Pick the John Deere 1025R if the mid-mount mower matters most, the Mahindra eMAX 25L HST for the strongest loader, or the LS MT125 for the most lift per dollar.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the difference between a subcompact and a compact tractor?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Sub compact tractors run about 20 to 25 hp, weigh roughly 1,400 to 1,900 lb and often have a limited Category 1 hitch; they are built to mow and carry a loader. Compact utility tractors run about 25 to 45 hp, weigh more and have a full Category 1 hitch for ground-engaging implements like tillers and rotary cutters.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How many acres can a sub compact tractor handle?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Kioti pitches its CS series for properties up to 10 acres, and that is a fair range for the class: two to ten acres of lawn, gardens and a gravel drive. More acreage is fine for mowing, but pasture, brush and field work push you toward a heavier compact tractor.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Can a sub compact tractor use Category 1 implements?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Yes, within limits. Most sub-compacts have a limited Category 1 hitch that accepts standard Category 1 implements, but lift capacity and weight restrict you to lighter ones: 4 to 5 foot box blades and land planes, 4 foot rotary cutters, small tillers, rear blades and post hole diggers.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How much can a sub compact tractor loader lift?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Manufacturer ratings on this page range from about 675 lb to 1,008 lb, but the measuring point matters. At 500 mm forward of the pivot, where a bucket's load actually sits, Deere's 120R loader is rated at 553 lb and Kubota's LA344 at about 509 lb, roughly 30 percent below the pivot-pin numbers.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is a sub compact tractor good for mowing?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Yes. The Kubota, Deere, Mahindra and LS here all offer 60-inch mid-mount decks driven by the mid PTO, and a sub-compact on turf tires handles uneven ground well. A zero turn mows faster, but a tractor that mows and also carries a loader replaces two machines on a property that needs both.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Can you buy a sub compact tractor on Amazon?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                No. The Kubota, John Deere, Mahindra, LS and Kioti tractors on this page are sold through dealers, and Amazon listings under their model numbers are parts, filters and seat covers. A dealer handles setup, warranty work and parts, which you will want on a tractor regardless.
              </p>
            </div>

          </div>
